---
/**
 * Regulation — third biology-lens concept at Collective scale.
 * Multi-speed coordination and damping of a specialized multicellular form.
 * Completes: Gene…Metabolism | Signal…Coupling | Multicellularity…Regulation.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Regulation | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Collective Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Regulation
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					Multi-speed coordination of a specialized multicellular form:
					how the whole stays coherent under load without erasing member Cells.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: organismal regulation / physiological control systems.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Completes Collective after
						<a href="/framework/multicellularity" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Multicellularity</a>
						and
						<a href="/framework/specialization" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Specialization</a>.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Keeping the differentiated whole alive.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, a multicellular organism with specialized tissues cannot survive on open exchange alone.
					<strong class="text-white/85">Regulation</strong> is the set of control processes that coordinate members across different speeds:
					fast local responses, slower systemic set-points, feedback that damps destructive oscillation and preserves the form of the whole.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, Regulation names that role under the biology lens.
					After the collective form exists
					(<a href="/framework/multicellularity" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Multicellularity</a>)
					and roles diverge
					(<a href="/framework/specialization" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Specialization</a>),
					Regulation is how the whole stays coherent under tension, load, and change
					without collapsing into one Cell or exploding into uncoupled parts.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the physics lens this is close to
					<a href="/framework/damping" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Damping</a>
					at collective scale: protection of coherence. Regulation is the living-form reading of multi-speed control, not a shipped set of agent modules.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Regulation is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Coordination of the whole:</strong> specialized members stay aligned to collective continuity.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Multi-speed control:</strong> fast local correction and slower systemic set-points can coexist.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Damping under load:</strong> reduces destructive oscillation without freezing all change.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Preservation of member Cells:</strong> regulation serves the collective form and the integrity of bounded members, not their erasure.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Regulation is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Specialization.</strong>
						Roles are the layout. Regulation is ongoing control of the differentiated whole.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Multicellularity itself.</strong>
						The higher-order form can exist before mature regulatory architecture.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a stack of agent modules.</strong>
						Nervous, immune, or hormonal systems are scientific readings of regulation.
						They are not Core Concepts to ship as separate Identity agents until Framework-derived.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not total control of members.</strong>
						Collective regulation is not Ownership of every Cell's Stem.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not pure stasis.</strong>
						Healthy regulation allows adaptation; freezing all change is pathology, not the goal.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Biology lens complete</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Three scales, ten concepts</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-4 text-lg">
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Single:</strong>
						<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/cell" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Cell</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/metabolism" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Metabolism</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Interactive:</strong>
						<a href="/framework/signal" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Signal</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/recognition" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Recognition</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/coupling" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Coupling</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong class="text-white/85">Collective:</strong>
						<a href="/framework/multicellularity" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Multicellularity</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/specialization" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Specialization</a>
						→
						<strong class="text-white/90">Regulation</strong>
					</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					Regulation answers: <em class="text-white/75">how does a specialized collective stay coherent without erasing its members?</em>
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Coordinate without capture:</strong> collective control that leaves member Boundaries real.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Use more than one speed:</strong> not every correction belongs at the same timescale.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Damp destruction, not all motion:</strong> protect coherence while Causal Entropy under constraint remains possible.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Do not ship organ-agents early:</strong> vocabulary first; modules only when Framework-derived.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">organismal physiology / regulatory systems</strong>
						(feedback, multi-speed control, coherence of the differentiated whole).
						The biology lens for Single · Interactive · Collective is complete at concept-page level.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/specialization" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Specialization</a>
					<a href="/framework/damping" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Damping</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
